{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, Rental Items are Returned to the Store."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers process initiation and the first actionable step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2",
        "guard:b1->c0"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process. However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the initial conditional split for return methods. Guard captures one branch; overall flow and logic preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct correspondence to the counting/comparison step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4",
        "guard:b2->n5",
        "guard:b2->n7",
        "guard:b2->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process. However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process. Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards correctly split the three order-status scenarios described. Action n4 restates the block; acceptable redundancy."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the missing-item notification step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process. However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process. Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Redundant extraction of the damage-notification arm already covered in the previous block. Does not alter behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, if there are damaged items and additional charges, we temporarily take them out of inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the inventory removal step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "guard:b3->c2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process. However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the binary decision regarding missing item returns. Guard captures one path; behaviour unchanged."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicit termination statement mapped to both an action node and the structural end marker."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9",
        "guard:b4->n10",
        "guard:b4->n11",
        "action:n10",
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process. On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Splits the repair/discarded decision into branch, guards, and outcome actions. Fully preserves the source logic despite granular splitting."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order. If the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process. If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the final packing/storage routing step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The customer is then emailed with replacement charges, and the process is complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Closes the process with the final notification step."
    }
  ],
